            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gitana"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved this stuff. I used whole spices though, roasted them together on dry pan until you could smell the aroma and then ground them all up. Was perfect on chicken tandoori and pulav."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CheekyScoop2115"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I combined this recipe with one 14 oz can coconut milk, one can tomato paste (6oz), and 1 TBSP chicken bouillon paste. Whisked together and then poured over 6 boneless/skinless chicken thighs + 4 chicken breast tenderloins, all over a bed of one sliced onion. Cooked in the crockpot on high for 3.5 hrs.... MAGNIFICENT!!! My whole family loved it, including the kiddos (ages 13-5 yrs)! My husband asked me to repeat it next Sunday!! Thank you for this recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2025-04-07T05:34:27.464Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Neonred"
            },
            "reviewBody": "If taste is king, then this recipe needs adjustment.\nFirst of all, no cloves (it's perfum).\nSecond, use 1 green and 2 black cardamom pods not 1.5 teaspoons worth, the black ones are smoky, green more perfumy hence the former.\nLastly use 3/8 teaspoon nutmeg and 1/8 mace.\n\nBecause one of the ingredients is cinnamon, its recommended to add the garam masala at the end of cook time.",
            "datePublished": "2017-11-11T09:59:45.223Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "David Starnes"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I toasted my spices first. Idlis, roti, coconut chutney, chickpea coconut curry…. They all freeze pretty well, so I break the Idli steamer out, make my Garam masala, chick peas soaked overnight, w lentils soaked about 4 to 5 hours. I learned South Indian cooking from my neighbor, she wanted to learn French/Vietnamese…I call that a “fare” trade off:)?",
            "datePublished": "2024-09-15T19:18:12.940Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Roseline Hatchell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used it for a Keema recipe that was posted in AllRecipes. Since I didn't have any at home, I had all of the spices already in the cupboard to make the Keema recipe I found. \nVery authentic! Now that I know that the spices are roasted first then ground, I will probably do that for now on as I have them whole as well.",
            "datePublished": "2021-10-28T14:51:41.207Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Garam Masala is so good in so many dishes. I make a big batch and use it frequently. I love Turmeric and added an equal portion as the other main spices. The flavor and color are better with that addition.",
            "datePublished": "2022-08-29T23:20:36.450Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ian M"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Easy peasy. I toasted the spices after mixing to release some fragrance",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-09T17:44:34.083Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
